* Longitude East is minus!!
* Lat/Lon: Integer degrees, decimal minutes
* If lat/lon is negative, also specify decimal minutes as negative!
*
* sets up multiple crustal models using individual delay files.
* execute these commands after the sta command to get delays properly.
*
*set alternate stations (east side of san andreas) for bear valley & loma prieta
* default northern california gradient model
*
* 'crh' lines define the models:
* crh <model number> <model file name>
*
* 'nod' names define the circles for using the models
* nod <latitude integer degrees> <latitude decimal minutes> <longitude integer degrees> <longitude decimal minutes> <radius in km for full weighting> <radius in km additional to inner circle for mixed weighting> <model number to use>
*
* 'mul' line to state a mixed model defaulting to model number 1 if not matching any 'nod' circles
* mul t 1
*
*
crh 1 'grenz.crh'
mul t 1
*
